# The shortcut's board: `pin` puts a Notice into the file, and `posts` gives back what the file holds as dicts, of no
# type of the code's: the Notice goes in and no type comes out. `posts` returns what it read, so it uses it, and the
# file stands between the put and the get as on the clean side.

route club.files.Board
step Board()/Board()
step Board()/Board.pin
step Board()/Board.posts

line entry > Board()/Board() call
line entry > Board()/Board.pin call
line entry > Board()/Board.posts call
line Board()/Board() > Board@Board()/Board() value
line Board@Board()/Board() > Board()/Board.pin value
line Board@Board()/Board() > Board()/Board.posts value
known #new line Notice·notice > Board()/Board.pin value          # new-A
line Board()/Board.pin > Disk(self.path) own
line Disk(self.path) > Board()/Board.posts own

home Board@Board()/Board() Board()
known #new home Notice·notice Board()

side entry left
known #76 side Disk(self.path) between                         # Atlas: right, as if what posts returns were unused

# new-A: the parameter of a method the entry calls has lost its name
known #new extra line Notice > Board()/Board.pin value
known #new extra home Notice Board()
